A kernel that scores what its nearest RBF scores is that RBF, whatever its
Spearman. Exploratory under deviations D4; nothing here is confirmatory.

==========================================================================
RBF SURROGATE (EXPLORATORY, D4): churn, pca/12 qubits, 250/class, bw arm
==========================================================================
  For each quantum kernel: fit the closest RBF on training Gram matrices
  (no labels), run it through the same pipeline, compare out of sample.
  A difference near zero means the quantum kernel is functionally that RBF.

  setting      n  gamma (median)  in grid    d normAP                 95% CI          p
  angle-r1    20       3.981e-03 20/20         -0.0031     [-0.0095, +0.0033]     0.2935
  angle-r2    20       3.981e-03 20/20         -0.0036     [-0.0099, +0.0028]     0.1140
  iqp-r1      20       5.623e-03 20/20         +0.0021     [-0.0094, +0.0136]     0.7841
  iqp-r2      20       1.122e-03 20/20         +0.0069     [-0.0055, +0.0193]     0.3300

  By embedding family:
    angle  n=40  quantum minus surrogate: -0.0033 [-0.0076, +0.0010]   p 0.0577
           no detectable difference, and the interval is tight: this family is functionally an RBF kernel and should be described that way.
    iqp    n=40  quantum minus surrogate: +0.0045 [-0.0036, +0.0126]   p 0.7047
           no detectable difference, and the interval is tight: this family is functionally an RBF kernel and should be described that way.

  Fitted gammas span 1.00e-03 to 2.82e-01; the registered classical RBF grid spans 1e-03 to 1e+02.
  80/80 surrogates use a gamma inside the range the classical arm already searched.

