==========================================================================
  For each quantum kernel: fit the closest RBF on training Gram matrices
  (no labels), run it through the same pipeline, compare out of sample.
  A difference near zero means the quantum kernel is functionally that RBF.

  setting      n  gamma (median)  in grid    d normAP                 95% CI          p
  angle-r1    20       3.981e-03 20/20         +0.0003     [-0.0008, +0.0015]     0.0353
  angle-r2    20       1.585e-02 20/20         +0.0001     [-0.0009, +0.0010]     0.0681
  iqp-r1      20       5.623e-03 20/20         -0.0006     [-0.0023, +0.0011]     0.0973
  iqp-r2      20       6.310e-03 20/20         -0.0010     [-0.0027, +0.0008]     0.0897

  By embedding family:
    angle  n=40  quantum minus surrogate: +0.0002 [-0.0005, +0.0009]   p 0.0055
           the quantum kernel BEATS its own closest RBF. This is the only result in the project that could support quantum structure doing work, and it needs replication before it is believed.
    iqp    n=40  quantum minus surrogate: -0.0008 [-0.0019, +0.0004]   p 0.0224
           the quantum kernel is WORSE than its own closest RBF, so its structure is costing rather than earning.

  Fitted gammas span 1.00e-03 to 2.51e-01; the registered classical RBF grid spans 1e-03 to 1e+02.
  80/80 surrogates use a gamma inside the range the classical arm already searched.

